.Dd @MDOCDATE@
.Dt CLOWN-PRESENCE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm clown-presence
.Nd query the clown session presence index
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm clown presence list
.Op Fl -group Ar group-id
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -quiet
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm clown presence
queries the presence index \(em the clown\(->spinclass liveness seam (RFC-0014).
Every live clown writes a presence record under
.Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/clown/presence/ ,
its job-watch monitor (see
.Xr clown-job 1 )
refreshes the record on a ticker, and a clean shutdown removes it; a stale
record (one not refreshed within the freshness window) is pruned on read.
This command is the stable query surface for that index: a consumer \(em notably
spinclass's liveness probe \(em uses it instead of reading the on-disk JSON
directly, so the record schema and the freshness window stay clown's concern.
It is a pure read, available regardless of
.Ev CLOWN_DISABLE_JOB_WAKEUP
.Pq when disabled no records are written, so the listing is simply empty .
.Pp
A presence record is written only by a clown whose job-watch monitor is running:
the claude-family providers, not
.Fl -naked
or an exec-replacing provider, and not when
.Ev CLOWN_DISABLE_JOB_WAKEUP Ns = Ns Ql 1 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Nm clown presence list
List the live presence records.
By default the output is a human listing grouped by
.Sy decoration
(the group-id), each line showing a record's per-instance key and description \(em
the same shape as
.Nm clown chat list .
.Fl -group
restricts the listing to records whose
.Sy decoration
.Pq the group-id, Ev CLOWN_GROUP_ID , No e.g. a spinclass session's Ar repo Ns / Ns Ar branch
equals
.Ar group-id ;
passing
.Fl -group
with an empty value selects the ungrouped records.
.Fl -json
emits one JSON record per line
.Pq Li {sessionKey,channelId,decoration,description,lastSeen} .
.Fl -quiet
suppresses output and turns the command into a liveness predicate: it exits
.Sy 0
when at least one matching live record exists and
.Sy 1
when none do
.Pq Xr grep 1 Fl q No style ,
so a probe is
.Dl clown presence list --group \(dq$ID\(dq --quiet
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev XDG_STATE_HOME
Root of the presence directory
.Pq Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/clown/presence/ .
.It Ev CLOWN_GROUP_ID
The group-id a live clown records as its
.Sy decoration ;
.Fl -group
matches against it.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm clown presence list
exits
.Sy 0
on success
.Pq or, with Fl -quiet , No when a matching record is live ,
.Sy 1
on a read error
.Pq or, with Fl -quiet , No when no matching record is live ,
and
.Sy 2
on a usage error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clown-chat 1 ,
.Xr clown-job 1 ,
.Xr clownfile 5
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC-0014 (clown\(enspinclass awareness seam: group-id and presence) and RFC-0013
(clownfile, per-instance identity, and clown-owned chat).
